    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12457" root="درك" body-key="d">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرَكَ</span></b> , from which should be derived <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرَاكِ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرَّاكٌ</span>, is unused, though its noun <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">درك</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرْكٌ</span>
or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرَكٌ</span>, which latter (the more common of the
two) see below,] is used. (IB.) [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرَكَ</span> in Golius's
Lex. is evidently a mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَارَكَ</span>.]

